Audit (brief Priority 2): the QSF path — readQsf → canonical → mapCanonical →
schema → quality check → report — was traced field by field against what the
Rescript schema can hold. The causes found: a grid row's display logic was
attached to the column with the same number; quota conditions never converted
(the operator lookup came first), so a "quota met" branch applied to everyone
and QuotaNotMet read as met; SelectedChoicesCount, BlockRandomizer,
carry-forward, advanced randomization (anchors, subsets, undisplayed),
translations, choice images and graphic blocks, side-by-side columns,
DefaultChoices, DataVisibility, layout configuration, survey options and the
end-of-survey message id were lost or flattened; unknown piping stayed in the
text unreported; the children of an Authenticator were hidden behind a
never-true branch; element kinds the reader does not know were never
mentioned; and the report could not say, per element, what came across.

Fixes (Priority 3): every element the adapter or the mapper decides is an
inventory item — imported / partial / unsupported, with the reason — and the
report's new `fidelity` section counts them per feature, lists unresolved
references, assets with their hosting risk, languages and the file's element
table; the summary states the measured share. Row logic goes to the row;
quota conditions become count-against-limit (a group cell flagged partial);
choice counts, BlockRandomizer, carry-forward, anchors / pick / always_hide,
translations (through recordTranslation, origin import, in_review), option
imageUrl and asset listing, side by side as a composite grid with every
column, piping for ChoiceDescription / QuestionText / counts / displayed /
remaining with the rest reported, defaults, hidden, headerRepeat,
fieldLabelPosition, decimalPlaces, ValidURL, branding from survey options,
signature / PGR / bipolar / Likert homes, Authenticator children kept, SC
scoring and unknown kinds in the element table.

Verification (Priority 4): packages/import/src/verify.ts checks the result's
structure against the source (families, choices, rows, variable names, every
code, blocks, quotas; analysis compatibility as numbers) and walks it with
the engine under eight strategies — a look-ahead "deepest" walk that passes
screeners, first, last, five random seeds — reporting pages, questions,
loops, end status, refusals, exceptions and unreached questions with a reason
(by source / no walk). /api/import/analyze returns it for a new project; the
ImportCard shows the fidelity bar, the per-feature detail, unresolved
references, assets, languages, the element table and the engine check.

Corpus (Priority 5): three synthetic, sanitized QSF files (simple → screener
with logic, quotas, embedded data → complex tracker with loops, block
randomizer, SBS, PGR, images, ES/FR) in packages/import/corpus/qsf, built by
scripts/qsf-corpus-build.mjs; scripts/qsf-fidelity.mjs measures them, pins
the whole measurement in expected.json (--update), and takes --dir for real
exports. Measured: 93.3 % / 84.4 % / 75.9 % of elements as-is; runtime 6/6,
12/12, 26/27 questions reached (the one left is a block outside the source
flow); before the fixes the screener file screened out every walk (4/12).
No real client export was available, so these numbers are for the corpus
only — the report says so.

Tests: packages/import 49 (21 new; mutation-checked 25/25), import-engine
browser suite extended (UI mutations 2/2), pnpm -r test green, Studio
typecheck, guard audit and docs check clean. Report:
docs/DASHBOARD-OVERVIEW-QSF-FIDELITY-2026-10-11.md.

